{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2974","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2974","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2974\",\"parent_revision\":\"02c48e13731c058241c5ed2bb06cf5b87ba0e25fc930439927681003a56a359a\",\"root_revision\":\"02c48e13731c058241c5ed2bb06cf5b87ba0e25fc930439927681003a56a359a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P0\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nFor as long as the #2956 write/parse key-mismatch has existed, any backlog section written under a mismatched or unregistered heading may have been stored under an unknown__ prefixed key instead of the key an agent expects when reading that section by name (e.g. \\\"Resources\\\", \\\"Dependencies\\\"). Whether an agent that reads a named section and gets no match silently proceeds as if the section legitimately doesn't exist, or detects and reports the miss, is unverified and likely inconsistent across the different agents and code paths that read backlog item content. If any consumer treats a miss as \\\"this item has no Resources/Dependencies\\\" rather than investigating why expected content is absent, then every decision that consumer made based on that assumption \u2014 for the entire time this condition has existed \u2014 was made on silently incomplete information.\\n\\nThis must be audited before it can be closed: which agents and code paths read specific named sections, whether each one's read mechanism matches by raw storage key or by display-converted title, whether a miss is detected and surfaced or silently treated as absence, and how many currently-groomed backlog items actually have unknown__-keyed content that a consumer would have missed under the affected read paths.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: User specified: \\\"omg - this means that all the steps where agents are told to read section 'Resources', 'Dependencies' or whatever from the issue this whole time, that they need to make their next choices based on, they have been blind to these 'unknown__resources', 'unknown_dependencies' that may have existed, and if not existed, they would have just been like, oh - this task i am about to do has no resources or dependencies. this is a p0 issue dude\\\"\\n\\nEvidence gathered this session: rtica-assessor.md lines 38-41 reads `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view(sections=[\\\"description\\\", \\\"Impact Radius\\\", \\\"Fact-Check\\\"])` \u2014 an exact-name filter. Per backlog_view's own tool schema, a section name not present returns an error dict with `section_filter_miss=True` and `valid_sections` listing what's actually available \u2014 not fully silent at the tool level, but whether the calling agent's prompt checks for and acts on that signal (versus treating any non-content response as \\\"section doesn't exist, proceed\\\") is unverified per-agent. rtica-assessor.md line 45 has a partial safety net for its two named dependencies specifically (\\\"If either section is missing, you are running too early... Broadcast BLOCKED\\\"), but this is not confirmed true for every other consumer of named sections across the system (planning, task decomposition, other groomer subsections, human/agent review during implementation). No migration or backfill exists (confirmed this session \u2014 searched backlog_core and migration scripts) to re-key already-stored unknown__ content, so any item groomed before the #2956/#2964 fix may currently hold real Resources/Dependencies/etc. content invisible under the display name a consumer would query for. Related: #2956 (root cause), #2970 (long-term architecture fix).\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **p0: agents reading named backlog sections may silently treat mis-keyed (unknown__) content as absent, corrupting downstream decisions** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 architecture review with user, 2026-08-18\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Investigation Update 2026 08 20\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Verdict: NOT RESOLVED.** The core contract question \u2014 can a caller distinguish \\\"section genuinely absent\\\" from \\\"section exists but silently swallowed under a mis-keyed heading\\\" \u2014 is still answered no, even after #2956/#3040 landed.\\n\\n**Confirmed by direct reproduction** against current `main`: called the real `_filter_view_sections()` (`backlog_core/server.py`, ~line 1204) with two realistic `view_item`-shaped payloads \u2014\\n- Case A (section genuinely absent): `section_filter_miss: True`, `valid_names: ['story', 'Story']`\\n- Case B (section absent, but unrelated content exists under an unrecognizable heading that normalize-on-read can't heal): `section_filter_miss: True`, `valid_names: ['story', 'unknown__zorbulon_frobnication_ledger', 'Story', 'Zorbulon Frobnication Ledger']`\\n\\n`section_filter_miss` is identical (`True`) in both cases \u2014 no dedicated field, exception, or sentinel distinguishes them. The mis-keyed content's raw key leaks undecorated into `valid_names` but nothing flags it as such. No warning/telemetry fires on this read path either (the one existing warning, `operations._warn_unregistered_section`, only fires on write).\\n\\n**Root cause**: `_filter_view_sections`'s no-match branch (`server.py` ~1299\u20131320) folds every non-matching name into one generic `valid_names` list, discarding the distinguishing information (whether a given key is `unknown__`-prefixed / definitively unresolved) that was available at that point.\\n\\n**Proposed fix**: partition `valid_names` into recognized-canonical vs. `unknown__`-prefixed/unresolved, and add a structured signal (e.g. `unresolved_sections: [...]`) set whenever any `unknown__`-prefixed key exists in the raw sections, independent of whether it matches the request.\\n\\n**Blast radius**: confirmed for the plural `sections=[...]` filter path (`server.py::_filter_view_sections`, used by 1 agent \u2014 `rtica-assessor.md`). The singular `section=` filter (used by 13 files including 5 agents) has an analogous implementation in `operations.py::_apply_body_section_filter` (~line 2507) sharing the same result shape \u2014 this was **not** independently reproduced and should be verified before assuming the same fix applies there (per this repo's evidence-action-proportionality rule).\\n\\nFix in progress in a follow-up branch/PR.\\n\\n\\n**Fix up for review**: PR #3047 \u2014 adds an `unresolved_sections` signal to `_build_section_miss_error` (the shared sink both the plural and singular section-filter paths converge on, confirmed by grep to be the single call site for both \u2014 no separate operations.py change was needed). 17/17 new tests pass; full plugin suite 3366 passed (1 unrelated pre-existing failure, untouched by this change). Not closing this issue until the PR merges.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b9ea9b227dedcb4c3bea0177814523f13fe0d5d698f0732cc01ebbbe8ad57697\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPtXVGQ\"}"}